<title>FRANCE: Paris April '97 import traffic up 2.2 pct - ADP.</title>
<headline>Paris April '97 import traffic up 2.2 pct - ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>April 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 44,877 tonnes, an increase of 2.2 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>....The Paris airports April 1997 import traffic, in tonnes, by region, with percentage change on April 1996, was:</p>
<p>				Tonnes  Pct change</p>
<p>....Domestic		 2,136  down  9.6</p>
<p>....European Union	 5,674    up 12.3</p>
<p>....Non-EU Europe	  1,011    up  1.0</p>
<p>....North Africa	     871  down  5.2</p>
<p>....Sub-Saharan Africa   4,622    up  3.2</p>
<p>....North America	 13,625  down 12.9</p>
<p>....French territories   1,788    up 10.3</p>
<p>....Latin America	  2,030    up 16.7</p>
<p>....Middle East	    2,207  down  4.7</p>
<p>....Far East		10,913    up 24.1</p>
<p>....Total		   44,877    up  2.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
